{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/896746-werewolf-population-in-2nd-edition","id":896746,"title":"Werewolf Population in 2ND edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-23T06:35:16-07:00","id":896746,"title":"Werewolf Population in 2ND edition","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> Quick question regarding the population of the Forsaken and the Pure in 2nd. I k now that in 1st edition WtF the pure outnumbered the Forsaken quite a bit. Has this changed between editions. In my games its much more equal numbers but I couldn't find anything about it in the new book. Thanks in advance.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer: WtF Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon<br /> United States Sailor, First Responder,Ally, Bad Speller, Book Hoarder and all around Nerd.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2640-rx781a","name":"rx781a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:26:14-07:00","id":896793,"title":"","content":"Well two werewolves mating no longer produces a 'demon spawn' so I'd imagine forsaken numbers are up or make more sense. I didn't see any specific numbers on the pure however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:48:05-07:00","id":896808,"title":"","content":"I did not see it ether. I always thought that the population difference in 1st edition was a bit unfair. Thanks for the help Mr.F.I.X.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer: WtF Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon<br /> United States Sailor, First Responder,Ally, Bad Speller, Book Hoarder and all around Nerd.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2640-rx781a","name":"rx781a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T12:06:24-07:00","id":897044,"title":"","content":"Whatever you please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:38:00-07:00","id":897122,"title":"","content":"The pure population overgrowth was due to the forsaken (correct me if im wrong, ive been awake 35 hours) having essentially a massive civil war. Believe it was called the brotherhood war or something similar. According to 1st edition lore, the pure and forsaken fluctuate with whose in the lead as far as population goes. Being as its religious ideologies really (And largely incorrect according to pangea unleashed from what I can see), I think the better question would be what is the total werewolf population in the world. And to that end, probably a lot higher then 1st editions. Then again I'm thinking of house ruling that you can turn people with a bite, just for that legendary bit of fun, so my world may be more populated then the one you run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:51:41-07:00","id":897143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/896746-werewolf-population-in-2nd-edition?p=897122#post897122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pure population overgrowth was due to the forsaken (correct me if im wrong, ive been awake 35 hours) having essentially a massive civil war. Believe it was called the brotherhood war or something similar. According to 1st edition lore, the pure and forsaken fluctuate with whose in the lead as far as population goes. Being as its religious ideologies really (And largely incorrect according to pangea unleashed from what I can see), I think the better question would be what is the total werewolf population in the world. And to that end, probably a lot higher then 1st editions. Then again I'm thinking of house ruling that you can turn people with a bite, just for that legendary bit of fun, so my world may be more populated then the one you run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when you factor in Lunacy can make you Wolf-Blooded (and being bitten by a werewolf is likely to subject you to Lunacy), followed by that one Tell where you turn into a wolf, you already kinda can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:56:07-07:00","id":897148,"title":"","content":"Yeah I've considered that, and its something my wife really wants to do as she likes the whole &quot;create your own pack&quot; motif. Best example I have being teen wolf season 2, when derek started recruiting the outcasts of the town. &gt;.&gt; Actually was a fantastic werewolf dynamic back then. ANYWAY, im considering just cutting out the middleman. <br /> <br /> As an aside, can wolf blooded bite other wolf blooded and -theoretically- spread the tell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T06:14:42-07:00","id":898852,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sure, why not? The one that turns you into Urshul on the full moon causes lunacy anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:22:02-07:00","id":898944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/896746-werewolf-population-in-2nd-edition?p=898852#post898852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, sure, why not? The one that turns you into Urshul on the full moon causes lunacy anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> hahaha, wow, I didn't actually realise the implications of that. Yeah, wolf-blooded tells that cause lunacy in some fashion can spread wolf-bloodedness, but given they can't take Gauru and don't usually have the lunacy penalty higher primal urge can grant, they likely won't cause a dramatic failure on an npc unless your ST wanted it to happen anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:25:41-07:00","id":899002,"title":"","content":"Gonna add me a pack of wolf blooded to my game that assumed American werewolf in Paris was the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T22:01:48-07:00","id":900687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/896746-werewolf-population-in-2nd-edition?p=896793#post896793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well two werewolves mating no longer produces a 'demon spawn'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Was never happy with that mechanic, anyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/896746-werewolf-population-in-2nd-edition?p=897122#post897122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again I'm thinking of house ruling that you can turn people with a bite</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to use a similar house rule. The bite is ritually infused with some of the wolf's essence, which transfers to the human and makes them a Werewolf. I include a ritual, so that they don't go accidentally turning people into wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-27-2016, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T22:25:59-07:00","id":900700,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> a rite to make a mundance human a Wolf-Blooded sounds interesting. There already exists a rite that allows humans to shape shift into wolf form so why not make someone accepted into a pack of the blood through a ritualistic rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:28:22-07:00","id":900996,"title":"","content":"<b>The Welcoming of Blood (Pack Rite)</b><br /> This rite anoints a human to receive the blessings of the Warden Moon, and the bygone Great Wolf.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Insanity, Blood, Howling, Inflicting a Tell<br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> Fire-Touched on the Bible-Belt have long devised a festivity to &quot;reward&quot; their best human agents. The subject of the rite is normally bound to a chair as they are smeared with sigils with the blood of the ritualist, who generally wraps him with a wolf-pelt, bites him or similarly hold his eyes open with anachronistic devises better fit for an early asylum while his packmates, in Urhan form celebrate with dissonant howls. The climax of the ritual is reached when a mirror is broken while depicting the victim. (Presence+Expression)<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (Requires 10 successes, the subject may resist with Stamina+Resolve)<br /> <b>Success:</b> The next time that the character suffers Lunacy, it'll be a considered an automatic dramatic failure. Many rites finish with a ritualist's display of the Killing Form in front of the subject. The inflicted Tell, (generally Bitten) is gained, but others may apply depending on the ritemaster's ingenuity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:46:44-07:00","id":902746,"title":"","content":"Nyrufa I like your house rule and I may well steal it. Particularly because I love forsakens new ritual system (as a player and as an anthropologist).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T09:32:31-07:00","id":902763,"title":"","content":"As an aside, how much influence does the moon really have on who becomes a werewolf vs who doesn't, especially noting their new linneage via dark ages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:37:26-07:00","id":902981,"title":"","content":"Totally gonna steal that rite.<br /> Turning people into Wolf-blooded is an essential part of my werewolf's concept - making a nice, big family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:09:17-07:00","id":923600,"title":"","content":"Well, the first edition said that there were about half a million werewolves in the world which is a pretty huge number in world of darkness terms ( mummies, in contrast, are guesstimated at about a thousand). Adding more crazed wolf killing machines to the world and explaining that the human race is blissfully ignorant always seemed like a stretch to me. The whole point of having twice as many Pure, I believe, was to create a sense of fear and dread. Pure are to forsaken what forsaken are to regular humans, there was always a bigger pack of Pure out there howling for your blood, with more powerful spirit allies and greater ferocity. Maybe the intent was to bring a bit of the desperate struggle from Apocalypse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}